    {
      "_id": "foB8Eq2ZbbcKqPD8",
      "name": "Breath Weapons",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/sword.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Choose two breath weapons from the \"Chimaera Breath Weapon\" list.\n\nChimaera Breath Weapon. - Poison Spit {@recharge}. Ranged Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 30/45 ft., one creature. Hit:22 (5d8) poison damage. Hit or miss, the poison then splashes around. The target and each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) poison damage.\n\nIn addition, each creature hit by the poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw, or be poisoned until the end of the chimera's next turn.\n- Lightning Breath {@recharge}. The chimaera exhales a bolt of lighting at a creature within 30 feet of it. That creature must make a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (5d8) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a success. Afterwards, the bolt jumps to a second creature within 30 feet of the first target and then to a third creature within 30 feet of the second one.\n- Acid Breath {@recharge}. The chimaera ejects acid in a 20-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a DC l5 Dexterity saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nFurther more, any nonmagical armor made of metal that is hit by the acid corrodes. After receiving damage, the armor takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to armor class. If its penalty drops to -5, the armor is destroyed.\n- Ice Jet {@recharge}. The chimaera exhales a frigid beam of blue-white light forming a line 80 feet long and 5 feet wide in any direction it wants.  Each creature in the line must make a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 13 (3d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one and it becomes incapacitated until the start of the chimaera's next turn.\n- Fire Breath {@recharge}. The chimaera exhales fire in a 45-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed against a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 11 (2d10) fire damage and catch fire; until someone takes an action to douse the fire, the creature takes 5 (1d10) fire damage at the start of each of its turns.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
